    "body": "## Changes\n- Initialize fresh v3 workers directly with their pinned identity, without synthetic v1/v2 state, wake queues or migration backups.\n- Preserve strict validation for existing migrated workers and refuse partial/legacy evidence as fresh state.\n- Retain the current installer generation and its manifest-linked predecessor; prune only older verified generations after successful publication under the installer lock.\n- Preserve modified, unknown and symlink-containing history; leave operational receipts, sessions, memories and checkouts alone.\n\n## Verification\n- Worker and worker CLI suites pass.\n- Native initialization/migration regression tests pass.\n- 34 installer packaging/recovery tests pass in an isolated python:3.12-bookworm Linux container, including interruption recovery and retention regressions.\n\nStacked on #159. Separate from the birds' Rook-only delivery-policy work. Not deployed. This is the first lifecycle cleanup slice; broader legacy-code removal and operational receipt compaction remain.",
